    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">usignpdf vs HelloSign (Dropbox Sign)</h1>

    <p>HelloSign (now Dropbox Sign) was long the darling of the startup world for its clean API and simple interface. However, since its acquisition by Dropbox, the product has become increasingly focused on driving users into the broader Dropbox ecosystem.</p>

    <h2>Why consider an alternative?</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Pricing creep:</strong> Tiers have become more expensive, pushing out solo users.</li>
        <li><strong>Ecosystem push:</strong> Constant nudges to use Dropbox for file storage.</li>
        <li><strong>Simplicity:</strong> While simpler than DocuSign, usignpdf strips away even more of the UI chrome, focusing entirely on getting the signature placed.</li>
